# Dependencies
node_modules/

# Build output
dist/
build/
.next/
out/
coverage/

# TypeScript incremental build state
*.tsbuildinfo

# Note on package-lock.json: deliberately NOT ignored.
#
# CI (.github/workflows/ci.yml) runs `npm ci`, which requires a lockfile and
# fails without one. Since the repo has neither a root lockfile nor per-package
# ones committed, both `backend-ci` and `frontend-ci` cannot pass today. Lockfiles
# should be committed rather than ignored - `npm ci` is the reproducible install,
# and `npm install` in CI can silently drift from what was tested.
#
# That is a decision for the repo owner rather than something to slip into a
# feature branch, because the lockfiles this branch generated are large.

# Environment files - never commit real values
.env
.env.local
.env.*.local
!.env.example

# Logs
*.log
npm-debug.log*
yarn-debug.log*
yarn-error.log*

# Editor / OS
.DS_Store
Thumbs.db
.idea/
*.swp
